  "Question": "The average distance from Earth to the Sun is approximately 150 000 000 km. Which of the following expresses this in scientific notation?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(15\\times10^7\\ \\mathrm{km}\\)",
    "B": "\\(1.5\\times10^8\\ \\mathrm{km}\\)",
    "C": "\\(1.5\\times10^7\\ \\mathrm{km}\\)",
    "D": "\\(0.15\\times10^9\\ \\mathrm{km}\\)"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Moving the decimal point in 150 000 000 8 places to the left gives 1.5, so the result is \\(1.5\\times10^8\\); the coefficients in \\(15\\times10^7\\) and \\(0.15\\times10^9\\) are not between 1 and 10.",
